{#
  The iPhone Duo showcase, for the App Store featuring nomination's supplemental
  materials: one editorial page, the film and little else. The film is Track A of
  the Duo showcase, the Duo Studio cinematic (the folded phone, the unfold, the
  cookbook across the open display, Cook View with the phone stood as a tent and as
  a laptop, the real page turn, and the fold back to the start, 23.3 s, a seamless
  loop). The showcase's rights review marks Track A internal only, because the
  phone is Apple's own 3D model; it is published here on the owner's explicit
  instruction (2026-10-20). The files are the campaign's own web encodes of that
  exact edit, copied unchanged by scripts/build-media.mjs; the poster is its first
  frame (scripts/screens.json).

  The player is the browser's: it starts by itself, muted, and loops; its own
  controls are the way to pause, scrub or go full screen, so anyone who lands here
  with autoplay held back (Low Power Mode, say) still sees a player with a play
  button, not a picture. Under reduced motion or Save-Data the short script after
  the player keeps it from starting; the poster shows and the controls remain.
#}
